ull,"year":null,"weight":108,"yt":null,"src":"ensayos"}],"album_genres":[{"id":179627025938841,"type":"genre","name":"French Pop","n":14},{"id":187826504537370,"type":"genre","name":"Yé-yé","n":7},{"id":69305143563054,"type":"genre","name":"Chanson","n":7},{"id":104870489879640,"type":"genre","name":"European Music","n":2},{"id":37457307821633,"type":"genre","name":"Schlager","n":2},{"id":153170436375,"type":"genre","name":"Chamber Folk","n":2},{"id":258906480523511,"type":"genre","name":"Baroque Pop","n":1},{"id":223327500886715,"type":"genre","name":"Contemporary Folk","n":1},{"id":190318565344926,"type":"genre","name":"Folk Pop","n":1},{"id":119918662365550,"type":"genre","name":"Italo Pop","n":1},{"id":42147038712068,"type":"genre","name":"Country Pop","n":1},{"id":10205813290158,"type":"genre","name":"Beat","n":1}],"labels":[],"album_labels":[],"own_scenes":[],"scenes":[],"book_tracks":[],"mentions":[],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Death in 2024","body":"Françoise Hardy passed away on June 11, 2024, after a long and influential career that saw her recognized for her pioneering sound, predating the American Grunge scene by decades. \"France, France, while Hardy, whom the people of France called the grandmother of Grunge. She died on June 11, 2024.\"","year":2024,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Peaked Too Soon - Bands That Were Ahead of Their Time","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cy5SCQV0HAY"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Bob Hardy's Astrologer and Musician Aunt","body":"Françoise Hardy is Bob Hardy's aunt, with whom he collaborated on an almanac. She is noted for being both an astrologer and a musician. \"Then again, he's also worked on an Elmanac with his aunt, whose name is Francois Hardy. She's an astrologer as well as a musician.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Franz Ferdinand: In Their Own Words","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RWbKqqW78yg"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Diverse Career Beyond Music","body":"In addition to her musical career, Françoise Hardy was also an actor, was involved in the world of fashion and photography, and even became a professional astrologer, showcasing her diverse talents and interests. \"She was also an actor. She was involved in the world of fashion and photography. And she even became a professional astrologer.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Peaked Too Soon - Bands That Were Ahead of Their Time","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cy5SCQV0HAY"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Early Grunge Pioneer","body":"Decades before grunge became a recognized genre in the late 1980s, Françoise Hardy's music from 1964, particularly a song with low-tune distorted guitar and raw drums, led her to be called \"La Grande du Grunge\" (the grandmother of Grunge). \"She has also been called Lagrange du Grunge. Grunge didn't become a thing until at the earliest, the late 1980s.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Peaked Too Soon - Bands That Were Ahead of Their Time","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cy5SCQV0HAY"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"International Appeal and Accolades","body":"Hardy is considered a national treasure in France and garnered fans worldwide due to her ability to sing in English, German, and Italian, making her one of the best-selling singers in French history. \"She's considered a national treasure in France and has friends worldwide because she also sang in English and German and Italian. Hardy remains one of the best-selling singers in French history.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Peaked Too Soon - Bands That Were Ahead of Their Time","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cy5SCQV0HAY"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Ye-Ye Singer","body":"Françoise Hardy was a prominent Ye-Ye singer in the late 1950s and 1960s French rock scene, known primarily for her sentimental and melancholic ballads. \"Francis Hardy was a well-known Ye-Ye singer. She was known primarily for singing sentimental and melancholic ballads.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Peaked Too Soon - Bands That Were Ahead of Their Time","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cy5SCQV0HAY"}]}],"awards":[{"kind":"award","title":"Victoires de la Musique – Female artist of the year (2005)","body":"Won.","year":2005,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q16682527"}]}],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":234389846213950,"type":"album","name":"Françoise Hardy","list_id":32093215757431,"list":"Pitchfork: The 200 Best Albums of the 1960s","src":"musthear","rank":90,"year":1962,"note":null,"yt":"sIsvZXAdny0","scaruffi":null},{"id":234389846213950,"type":"album","name":"Françoise Hardy","list_id":167105581234386,"list":"RYM Top — Country — Country Pop","src":"musthear","rank":68,"year":1962,"note":null,"yt":"sIsvZXAdny0","scaruffi":null},{"id":234389846213950,"type":"album","name":"Françoise Hardy","list_id":108997246366764,"list":"RYM Top — Folk — Chamber Folk","src":"musthear","rank":112,"year":1962,"note":null,"yt":"sIsvZXAdny0","scaruffi":null},{"id":234389846213950,"type":"album","name":"Françoise Hardy","list_id":136210250045982,"list":"RYM Top — Pop — Folk Pop","src":"musthear","rank":103,"year":1962,"note":null,"yt":"sIsvZXAdny0","scaruffi":null},{"id":210500187513473,"type":"album","name":"Tous les garçons et les filles","list_id":118873104131320,"list":"RYM Top — Pop — French Pop","src":"musthear","rank":20,"year":1962,"note":null,"yt":"5cSFjJ4CJKc","scaruffi":null},{"id":234389846213950,"type":"album","name":"Françoise Hardy","list_id":118873104131320,"list":"RYM Top — Pop — French Pop","src":"musthear","rank":23,"year":1962,"note":null,"yt":"sIsvZXAdny0","scaruffi":null}